STRICT RULES
- Generate exactly {{ draft_count }} drafts. Not fewer, not more.
- Each draft MUST set `concept_no` to one of the concept_no values listed in the CONCEPT CATALOGUE, and `concept_uuid` to the matching concept_uuid. The pipeline rejects drafts that fail this check.
- Each draft MUST set `question_category` to either "NUMERICAL" (the question requires arithmetic / calculation / a numerical answer) or "THEORETICAL" (the question requires conceptual reasoning, definition recall, statement evaluation).
- Each draft MUST include `bloom` as an array of 1 or 2 entries, each `{bloom_level, bloom_priority}` where bloom_priority is 1 (primary) or 2 (secondary). Allowed bloom_level values: REMEMBER, UNDERSTAND, APPLY, ANALYZE, EVALUATE, CREATE. Stay within the bloom_levels_allowed list in CURRICULUM CONSTRAINTS.
- `question_text` is HTML. Wrap statements in `<p>...</p>`. Wrap inline math in `$...$`, display math in `$$...$$` (KaTeX-compatible). DO NOT include `<html>`, `<body>`, `<script>`, or `<style>` tags.
- `options` are required for option-based question types (MULTIPLE_CHOICE, ASSERTION_REASONING, MULTI_STATEMENT_MCQ, TRUE_FALSE, MATCH_COLUMNS). For TRUE_FALSE always emit exactly 2 options: `{A: True, B: False}`. For MULTIPLE_CHOICE emit exactly {{ curriculum_constraints.options_count_for_mcq | default(4) }} options. For non-option types (VERY_SHORT_ANSWER, SHORT_ANSWER, FILL_IN_THE_BLANK, LONG_ANSWER, CASE_STUDY, SUBPART_BASED) emit `options: []`.
- `correct_options` for option-based types contains the keys of the right option(s). For non-option types emit `correct_options: []` and put the model answer in `answer_text`.
- `answer_text` may be empty for pure option-based questions, or contain a one-line hint or the full model answer for descriptive types. HTML + KaTeX allowed.
- `question_mark` is the proposed marks (integer 1..10). Default 1 for MCQ / TRUE_FALSE / FILL_IN_THE_BLANK, 2 for VSA, 3 for SA, 5 for LA / CASE_STUDY. Tune to the difficulty.
- `question_diagram_url` is empty unless `metadata.include_visual_questions` is true AND the question genuinely requires a diagram from CHAPTER KNOWLEDGE; otherwise emit `""`.
- Use temp IDs: `draft_{{ metadata.batch_id }}_0001` .. `draft_{{ metadata.batch_id }}_{{ '%04d' | format(draft_count) }}`.
- Cite `source_section_ids[]` + `source_pages[]` per question (these come from CHAPTER KNOWLEDGE section ids and page numbers).
- Forbidden phrases (must not appear anywhere): {{ curriculum_constraints.forbidden_patterns | tojson }}
- Use facts ONLY from CHAPTER KNOWLEDGE. Any answer not grounded there is a hallucination and will be rejected by AI Call 2.
- Output JSON ONLY. No prose. No markdown. No code fences.
